==Japanese==
{{ja-kanjitab|たの|yomi=k}}

===Etymology===
{{IPAfont|⟨tano<sub>1</sub>siki<sub>1</sub>⟩}} → *{{IPAchar|/tanʷosikʲi/}} → {{IPAchar|/tanoshii/}}

From {{inh|ja|ojp|-|sort=たのしい}}. First attested in the ''{{w|Kojiki}}'' of 712 {{CE}}.<ref>{{R:Nihon Kokugo Daijiten 2|楽}}</ref> No Ryukyuan cognates exist; as as result, further derivation {{unk|ja|nocap=1}}. Theories include:
* A compound of {{m|ja|手|tr=ta|t=hand|pos=combining form}} + {{m|ja|伸す|tr=nosu|t=to extend}}
*: This is problematic, as ''nosu'' has first been attested starting from the early 900s, with no A/B distinction (see {{w|Jōdai Tokushu Kanazukai}} for details).
* From {{m|ja|田神|tr=tano|lit=rice paddy god}}
*: No reading of {{m|ja|神|tr=*no|t=god}} exists.
* A borrowing from an unknown language
*: No words resemble ''*tanV'' meaning "fun" or "to enjoy".

